1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,550
January 22, 1879. At a tiny British outpost

2
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:07,950
called Rorke's Drift, about 150 soldiers

3
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:09,200
got terrible news.

4
00:00:09,798 --> 00:00:11,188
Just six miles away,

5
00:00:11,418 --> 00:00:13,538
the Zulu army had wiped out a British force

6
00:00:13,538 --> 00:00:16,578
at Isandlwana. More than 1,300 men were

7
00:00:16,578 --> 00:00:16,968
dead.

8
00:00:17,448 --> 00:00:20,068
And now, up to 4,000 Zulu warriors were

9
00:00:20,068 --> 00:00:21,198
heading straight for them.

10
00:00:21,695 --> 00:00:23,535
Dozens of the defenders were sick in the

11
00:00:23,535 --> 00:00:25,045
hospital. They could have run.

12
00:00:25,375 --> 00:00:25,845
They stayed.

13
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:27,410
In about an hour,

14
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:29,420
they built walls out of maize sacks and

15
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:30,190
biscuit boxes.

16
00:00:30,809 --> 00:00:32,119
Then the attack began.

17
00:00:32,582 --> 00:00:34,812
Wave after wave charged the barricades.

18
00:00:35,382 --> 00:00:36,992
When the hospital was set on fire,

19
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:39,002
soldiers hacked holes through its walls

20
00:00:39,002 --> 00:00:40,652
and dragged the patients out,

21
00:00:40,922 --> 00:00:41,852
room by room.

22
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:43,360
They fought through the night,

23
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:44,630
by the light of the flames.

24
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:48,030
Of 20,000 rounds, only 900 were left.

25
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:50,500
At dawn, the Zulu army withdrew.

26
00:00:50,997 --> 00:00:52,807
17 defenders were dead.

27
00:00:53,417 --> 00:00:56,267
Around the walls lay 350 Zulu warriors.

28
00:00:57,034 --> 00:00:59,224
Eleven men received the Victoria Cross.

29
00:00:59,674 --> 00:01:01,804
The most ever awarded for a single battle.

30
00:01:02,404 --> 00:01:03,164
Would you have stayed?

31
00:01:03,164 --> 00:01:05,524
Follow Buried Chronicles for more forgotten

32
00:01:05,524 --> 00:01:06,054
history.

